><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>There is robust evidence in the literature to suggest that when&#xD;carefully planned, oral NaHCO</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>3 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>supplementation between 0.2 and&#xD;0.4 g/kg BW can improve athlete performance by ~2% to 3%.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>4</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>5&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The current investigation failed to observe any changes in blood&#xD;buffering capacity resulting from topical NaHCO</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>3 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>application in a&#xD;concentration equivalent to 0.3 g/kg BW, and no ergogenic effect&#xD;on performance was evident. Given these observations, we advise&#xD;that oral ingestion rather than topical application of NaHCO</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>3&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>remains the preferred supplementation method for increasing blood&#xD;buffering capacity and potentially improving performance tasks&#xD;1 to 7 minutes in duration.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>4</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>5 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Accordingly, and given the recognized&#xD;GI issues that accompany the use of this supplement, athletes&#xD;should aim to individualize their supplementation protocol in an&#xD;attempt to maximize the ergogenic effect while minimizing GI&#xD;discomfort. However, as with any dietary supplement, consultation&#xD;with a sports nutrition professional is strongly advised prior to&#xD;inclusion in an athlete’s nutrition plan.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>1</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>28</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
